<title>JAPAN: Yamaha shares touch new high for financial year.</title>
<headline>Yamaha shares touch new high for financial year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yamaha Corp extended gains on Friday morning, reaching a new high for this financial year.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the major musical instruments maker, which is diversifying its business into semiconductors, said it had signed an original equipment manufacturing (OEM) contract with Xicor Inc of the United States to make semiconductor chips for the U.S. firm.</p>
<p>At 0048 GMT, the share was up 60 yen at 2,190, above its previous high for the year that started last April 1 of 2,160, marked on Thursday. Volume was 721,000 shares.</p>
